From b521c0fe041e9518d357c9f53f3767dc51e3af22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johan Hovold <johan+linaro@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 18 Nov 2024 12:42:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 042/105] wip: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e78100-t14s: enable
 bluetooth

Adapt Stephan Gerhold's work to enable Bluetooth on the CRD to the T14s:

    Add the WiFi/BT nodes for CRD and describe the regulators for the
    WCN7850 combo chip using the new power sequencing bindings.

    Unlike QCP, CRD has the WCN7850 chip on a removable M.2 card. In
    this case, there is only a standard 3.3V and 1.8V supply that we
    need to turn on (plus the two enable GPIOs). The other voltages
    (0.95V and 1.9V) are derived on the M.2 card, by regulators that are
    not part of the CRD mainboard.

    Right now the bindings require describing all of these regulators.
    We need new bindings to describe these M.2 cards with only the two
    actual supplies.  For now just copy the necessary additions from
    QCP. Functionally this works correctly for CRD, because from a
    hardware perspective we need to do exactly the same for both devices
    (toggle the GPIO to get the supplies up).

Signed-off-by: Johan Hovold <johan+linaro@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Neil Armstrong <neil.armstrong@linaro.org>
Signed-off-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
